// **The Worker `yokohama-web` at the OPEN door** (R-6.5c2.39) — the state-1
// configuration of the door window: `wrangler.jsonc` with no identity service.
// Anyone who reaches the Worker plays under any name, so it is deployed for
// the window and never left live: `npm run deploy:open` ships it, and the
// plain `npm run deploy` reverts to the worker door (`worker/RUNBOOK.md` §19
// is the window's record; `worker/README.md` "The two doors" is the recipe).
//
// Everything but the door and the Turnstile declaration is `wrangler.jsonc`'s —
// the route, the assets block, the object bindings, the migration, the bucket,
// the archive and both TTLs — and the deploy guard holds it to production's
// blocks (checks 5 and 6) and to its `vars` but those (T8-a):
// `node scripts/deploy-guard.mjs --config wrangler.open.jsonc`. Its
// `YOKOHAMA_TURNSTILE` is `on` (cycle F, R-FP4), so the guard refuses it over
// a client built without the site key: the window builds a keyed client
// first. It has no `ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN` or `ACCESS_AUD` (the open door reads
// neither) and no `YOKOHAMA_DEV_DOOR`, which the shell refuses beside `open`
// (`src/config.ts`'s `openDoorRefusals`).
//
// THE OPERATOR SECRET MUST BE DELETED BEFORE THIS DEPLOYS. `YOKOHAMA_WEB_ADMINS`
// and `DEV_DOOR_CLIENT_ID` are Worker secrets, which a deploy leaves alone, and
// the shell refuses the open door beside an operator list: delete both
// (`wrangler secret delete`), deploy this, and put them back on the revert.
{
  "$schema": "./node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "yokohama-web",
  "main": "src/index.ts",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-15",
  "routes": [{ "pattern": "yokohama.moore.nyc", "custom_domain": true }],
  // No Access application stands in front of an open deployment, so a
  // `workers.dev` URL would go around nothing; it stays off all the same, and
  // the window is one hostname.
  "workers_dev": false,
  "preview_urls": false,
  "observability": { "enabled": true },
  "rules": [{ "type": "CompiledWasm", "globs": ["**/*.wasm"], "fallthrough": true }],
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./assets",
    "binding": "ASSETS",
    "html_handling": "none",
    "not_found_handling": "404-page",
    "run_worker_first": ["/api/*", "/enter"]
  },
  "durable_objects": {
    "bindings": [
      { "name": "TABLE", "class_name": "Table" },
      { "name": "HOUSE", "class_name": "House" },
      { "name": "ARCHIVER", "class_name": "Archive" }
    ]
  },
  "migrations": [{ "tag": "v1", "new_sqlite_classes": ["Table", "House", "Archive"] }],
  "r2_buckets": [{ "binding": "ARCHIVE", "bucket_name": "yokohama-archive" }],
  // Two Rate Limiting bindings (security S2b, finding C2; decision D-3), counted per Cloudflare location by the
  // key `src/limits.ts` derives: a caller's digest under `worker`; under `open` the connecting IP for a create and
  // IP plus claim for a write. The figures: ten creates a minute is a person opening tables as fast as a form
  // allows; a hundred and twenty writes per ten seconds is twelve a second, thirty times a fast player's four — the
  // local two-browser walk's pages peak at 71 unsafe requests in 10 s at machine speed (measured at S2b's pre-flight;
  // the live tier is slower, never faster), and the live replay, which sends 26 rows at the production door since
  // S1b, never reaches it. A `namespace_id` is a string here and unique to the ACCOUNT,
  // and a shared id shares counters across Workers. The deploy guard's check 13 holds this block to these literals,
  // and the pool's two files to the two NAMES, with a lenient figure of their own.
  "ratelimits": [
    { "name": "CREATE_LIMIT", "namespace_id": "7301", "simple": { "limit": 10, "period": 60 } },
    { "name": "WRITE_LIMIT", "namespace_id": "7302", "simple": { "limit": 120, "period": 10 } }
  ],
  "vars": {
    "YOKOHAMA_WEB_IDENTITY": "open",
    "YOKOHAMA_WEB_ARCHIVE": "r2",
    "YOKOHAMA_WEB_TABLE_TTL_DAYS": "90",
    "YOKOHAMA_WEB_OPEN_TABLE_TTL_DAYS": "7",
    "YOKOHAMA_WEB_LOBBY_CHAT": "on",
    "YOKOHAMA_WEB_CHAT_KEEP": "500",
    "YOKOHAMA_WEB_CHAT_TEXT": "500",
    // The Turnstile DECLARATION (cycle F, R-FP2, R-FP4; spec §2.6): `on` — the
    // window ships a client built WITH the site key, and the zone's edge rule
    // (`scripts/edge-rule.mjs`) challenges every path that is not the
    // release's own. The Worker reads nothing of it but that it is a string:
    // the deploy guard's check 12 refuses it over a keyless build, and the
    // smoke's live mode then requires a cookie-less `GET /api/health` answered
    // 403 `cf-mitigated: challenge`.
    "YOKOHAMA_TURNSTILE": "on"
  }
}
